   :summary
   "- Version change: 2.0 → 3.1.1.\n- Major contractual differences:\n  - Domestic content obligations and the Domestic Content Grids (Appendix C) present in v2.0 are removed in v3.1.1 — material (high importance) for suppliers subject to domestic-content compliance.\n  - v3.1.1 introduces and requires use of a \"Prescribed Form\" (defined in Appendix A) for notices, amendments, contact updates and termination notices — administrative (medium importance).\n  - v3.1.1 broadens stated disclosure purposes to include public health & safety and emergency-planning uses — privacy/data-sharing (low-medium importance).\n- Core pricing/indexing, LDC payment guarantee, metering and connection-related obligations remain unchanged.\n- Recommended next steps:\n  1. Confirm whether domestic content obligations are enforced elsewhere (microFIT Rules or OPA policy) or removed; obtain written clarification if required.\n  2. Obtain the OPA 'Prescribed Form' from the OPA Website and update internal processes to use it for all Notices/Amendments/Contact changes/Terminations.\n  3. Update privacy / disclosure expectations and record-retention to reflect expanded disclosure uses.\n  4. If you rely on domestic content credits or need to demonstrate compliance, preserve copies of v2.0 and any related documentation until clarification is obtained."},
